usiness_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1}],"text":[{"business_id":"npt8cAWD2lpu9QCEpeS55g","review_id":"0GtdWx62DxkEj-oOMiDt9Q","date":"2014-03-24T16:56:25","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9420464634895325,"text_excerpt":"Good Irish food. We came here because we were burnt out on the quarter. We wanted something close to our b&b so we walked here. The bangers and mash were very good and filling. My wife had a salad that she said was very good however it was a salad. We also had the bread pudding which was good with the cream topping and the caramel sauce. Nothing spectacular though. A little pricey for the food but the service was very good. They were very empty the night we ate there so that helped with the service. They have a huge selection if Irish whiskey and beer. I don't drink either but I bet it is all excellent."},{"business_id":"npt8cAWD2lpu9QCEpeS55g","review_id":"ib9QVlNBSMlM6h88YCQ47Q","date":"2011-12-05T15:53:28","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9382811784744263,"text_excerpt":"Having arrived into town rather late last night (a Sunday, at that) and hungry, but too tired to do more than walk a block for edibles, I found myself at the Irish House. What a sparkling place! It's an elegant, friendly pub. Although they only had their bar menu available at this hour, I found two things I could order and chose the lesser of two (deep fried) evils: the mushrooms (I was tempted to get the chips, too. Don't think I wasn't!) Add in a couple glasses of Malbec (they have a good selection of wines by the glass), some really nice service and yep, I'm a fan of the Irish House."},{"business_id":"npt8cAWD2lpu9QCEpeS55g","review_id":"fud4xW1miVZEj6_ENQURhw","date":"2012-06-04T21:27:13","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9369949698448181,"text_excerpt":"I really enjoy this place. The food is always good, if not excellent, and the drinks (particularly the beer/Guinness) is wonderful. It's a comfortable, fun, and relaxed atmosphere with great live music at certain times. The gift shop of Irish specialties is fun, as well. The brunch on Saturday and Sunday is very nice and very inexpensive. I love the full Irish breakfast, even some items on it are perhaps a little strange for many American tastes. We go here usually once a week or so, so I'm obviously a fan."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"npt8cAWD2lpu9QCEpeS55g","photo_id":"2xHfOZ9m8ZJ31w6QfQCyXQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/2xHfOZ9m8ZJ31w6QfQCyXQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9089903831481934},{"business_id":"npt8cAWD2lpu9QCEpeS55g","photo_id":"dkt9BC2pXbyfRL8Ak-_Qpw","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/dkt9BC2pXbyfRL8Ak-_Qpw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9089903235435486}]},"notebook_case":null}
